  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "For the reaction of hydrochloric acid and sodium carbonate",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Na**<sub>**2**</sub>**CO**<sub>**3**</sub>** (s) + 2HCl (aq) → 2NaCl (aq) + H**<sub>**2**</sub>**O (l) + CO**<sub>**2**</sub>** (g)**",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "1. Measure out a fixed volume of hydrochloric acid, e.g. 25.0 cm<sup>3</sup>, into a conical flask\n2. Add a known mass of sodium carbonate, e.g. 0.05 g, to the conical flask\n3. Immediately connect the gas syringe delivery tube\n4. Allow the reaction to go to completion\n5. Record the volume of carbon dioxide produced\n6. Repeat the experiment with different masses of sodium carbonate, e.g. 0.10 g, 0.15 g, 0.20 g, 0.25 g... 0.50 g\n7. Some assumptions are made about the experiment:",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The amount of gas lost between adding the sodium carbonate and connecting the delivery tube is negligible",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000015",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The delivery tube set up is airtight so no gas is lost",
    "reading_order" : 15,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The reaction does go to completion",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000017",
